== 12. Of Adoption

#speech[#smallcaps[Paragraph 1]: All those that are justified, God vouchsafed, in and for the sake of His only Son Jesus Christ, to make partakers of the grace of adoption,#footnote[Eph 1:5; Gal 4:4–5] by which they are taken into the number, and enjoy the liberties and privileges of the children of God,#footnote[John 1:12; Rom 8:17] have His name put on them,#footnote[2 Cor 6:18; Rev 3:12] receive the spirit of adoption,#footnote[Rom 8:15] have access to the throne of grace with boldness, are enabled to cry Abba, Father,#footnote[Gal 4:6; Eph 2:18] are pitied,#footnote[Ps 103:13] protected,#footnote[Prov 14:26; 1 Pet 5:7] provided for,#footnote[Heb 12:6] and chastened by Him as by a Father,#footnote[Isa 54:8–9] yet never cast off,#footnote[Lam 3:31] but sealed to the day of redemption,#footnote[Eph 4:30] and inherit the promises as heirs of everlasting salvation.#footnote[Heb 1:14; 6:12]]
